\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces TBR as a function of \ce {^6Li} enrichment percentage (starting at 5\%). The curve is characterised by a rapid initial increase which saturates early; the ``knee" of the curve appears at approximately 20\%, with the TBR effectively capping at 40\%. Beyond this saturation point, the returns are diminishing. Notably, a slight suppression in breeding performance is observed at near-total enrichment levels ($>90\%$)}}{12}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:enrichment}{{5}{12}{TBR as a function of \ce {^6Li} enrichment percentage (starting at 5\%). The curve is characterised by a rapid initial increase which saturates early; the ``knee" of the curve appears at approximately 20\%, with the TBR effectively capping at 40\%. Beyond this saturation point, the returns are diminishing. Notably, a slight suppression in breeding performance is observed at near-total enrichment levels ($>90\%$)}{figure.caption.7}{}}
