\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Analysis of breeder blanket radial thickness. On the left, TBR is plotted against average blanket thickness. TBR saturates at approximately 500 mm, suggesting full neutron attenuation. The cross-sectional heatmap of reaction density is plotted on the right. The reaction rate drops to negligible levels beyond the $640-580=60$cm depth into the blanket, confirming the saturation thickness observed from the left graph. The vast majority of the reactions occur near the surface, up to $\sim $ 20cm depth.}}{16}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:blanket_thicknesses}{{10}{16}{Analysis of breeder blanket radial thickness. On the left, TBR is plotted against average blanket thickness. TBR saturates at approximately 500 mm, suggesting full neutron attenuation. The cross-sectional heatmap of reaction density is plotted on the right. The reaction rate drops to negligible levels beyond the $640-580=60$cm depth into the blanket, confirming the saturation thickness observed from the left graph. The vast majority of the reactions occur near the surface, up to $\sim $ 20cm depth}{figure.caption.12}{}}
